# [[.Title]]

[[.Title]] is a Go web app built on [C4Stack](https://github.com/coolapso/c4stack):
Gin, Templ, HTMX and PostgreSQL, with Hanko for sign-in.

## Run it locally

You need Go, [Task](https://taskfile.dev) 3.51.1 or later, and Docker.

1. Create a [Hanko Cloud](https://cloud.hanko.io) project with `http://localhost:8080`
   as its app URL, and put its API URL in `.env` as `[[.EnvPrefix]]_HANKO_API_URL`.
2. Start the database and apply migrations:

   ```sh
   task db:up db:migrate
   ```
3. Start the app with live reload, then open http://localhost:8080:

   ```sh
   task dev
   ```

`task --list` shows every task. `go run . help` shows the app's commands.

## Where things are

| Path | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `main.go` | The app's wiring: modules, migrations and the server |
| `config.go` | Settings from `[[.EnvPrefix]]_*` environment variables |
| `routes.go` | What is served where |
| `layout.go`, `pages.templ`, `static/` | The design and pages |
| `migrations/` | The app's database migrations |
| `Taskfile.yml` | The app's tasks; shared ones come from C4Stack |

## Configuration

| Variable | Required | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_PUBLIC_URL` | yes | The origin users reach the app on |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_DATABASE_URL` | yes | PostgreSQL URL; the only setting `migrate` reads |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_SECRET_KEY` | yes | At least 32 bytes; signs CSRF tokens and seals cookies |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_HANKO_API_URL` | yes | The Hanko tenant's API URL |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_ADDR` | no | Listen address, `:8080` by default |
| `[[.EnvPrefix]]_LOG_LEVEL`, `[[.EnvPrefix]]_LOG_FORMAT` | no | `debug`…`error`; `json` (default) or `text` |

## Deploy

Build and push the image with `task container:push REGISTRY=…`. On each release:

1. Run the image with the `migrate` command as a one-off job. It needs only
   `[[.EnvPrefix]]_DATABASE_URL`.
2. Roll out the image with the `serve` command. Point readiness probes at
   `/health/ready` and liveness probes at `/health/live`.

## Upgrade C4Stack

```sh
task framework:update VERSION=vX.Y.Z
```

This moves the Go dependency and the shared tasks to the new release, then regenerates,
tests and builds. Read the release notes, then run `task db:migrate`.
